{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And Jacob vowed a vow, saying.</b> The meaning is that he uttered the vow with his lips, for otherwise a vow in the heart alone is not a vow." "<b>If He will be, etc.</b> This word ״אִם״ is to be interpreted according to what they of blessed memory said (Bava Kamma, chapter 4, mishnah 5) concerning the verses (Exodus 21:30) ״אִם כֹּפֶר״, ״אִם כֶּסֶף תַּלְוֶה״ (Exodus 22:24) — that it is not a doubt but a certainty, as though he had said ״כַּאֲשֶׁר יִהְיֶה זֶה״, etc. (Mekhilta, end of Parashat Yitro)." "<b>Further,</b> it intends along this line: if the attribute of strict justice will agree to the matter — and this is what he means by <b>if Elohim will be</b>. For He had spoken to him only from the attribute of mercy, as it is written ״וְהִנֵּה ה׳ נִצָּב וְגוֹ׳ הִנֵּה אָנֹכִי עִמָּךְ״, and it is well known that the attribute of mercy consents to bestow good while the attribute of strict justice withholds the matter. Therefore he said ״אִם יִהְיֶה אֱלֹהִים״, etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:21.373856833Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}